The Lord uses Peter to bring salvation to Cornelius and his household. This experience also teaches Peter, and the other Jewish believers with him, an important theological truth: the Lord accepts people from every nation and his offer of salvation is the same for all people. As reinforcement of this truth, the Gentiles experience the gift of the Holy Spirit in the same way that the Jews had at Pentecost ({Acts 2:4};&nbsp;{Acts 10:47}).&nbsp;

